Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Document reader: a pay stub fills and checks the 401(k),
 Roth part and match

What the person sees (owner's request 2026-11-11: "maybe they didn't input how much they
contributed ... the match"): paste the latest pay stub and the reader shows, apart, the
401(k) money you pay the tax on later, the Roth 401(k) money you pay the tax on now, and the
employer's match when the stub prints it. Each is a proposal with what is on file now and
what it would become, a paycheck and a year, applied only on "Use it". A 401(k) nobody typed
(Casey's empty row, or no row at all) is filled or made, with a $0 account for a Roth 401(k)
at work. Opened from #/ai/reader?kind=paystub (&person=<id>) the page starts on a pay stub.
Works on the phone with no AI and no PC (pasted text, labels only). Account numbers are never
read or kept, and the page says so.

Formulas and decisions:
- Three fields read apart: k401 = a 401(k)/401K/403(b) line that does not say Roth, match,
  employer, ER, company, loan or after-tax (the old pattern read "ROTH 401K" as pre-tax);
  roth401k = "Roth 401(k)", "401K Roth" or a Roth line that is not the match, a loan or an IRA;
  match = ER/employer/company match lines. A number followed by % is a rate, never money.
- A year = perYear(amount a paycheck, period) (52, 26, 24 or 12); employerMatch is yearly:
  perYear(match a paycheck, period), to the cent. A stub that does not say how often you are
  paid gets a "How often are you paid?" box.
- workRows: the person's first row into a 401k account (later) and into a roth account that
  limitKind counts as a 401(k) (now); a former job's account is never this paycheck's. A missing
  row is made at use, into an account of that kind the person owns, else a new $0 account
  "<Name>'s 401(k) at work" / "<Name>'s Roth 401(k) at work" (the "401(k)" in the name keeps the
  401(k) limit, IRC 402A(c)(2)). Rows are looked up again at each use: any tap order gives one
  account of each kind.
- D-C1 words: "pay the tax later" / "pay the tax now". D-C2: the match always lands on the
  pay-the-tax-later row (IRC 402(a); a Roth match is optional, SECURE 2.0 s.604); a match typed
  on the Roth row moves there, never counted twice; a Roth-only stub with a pre-tax row on file
  offers $0 for that row ("use it if the money on file is the same Roth money").
- Using money going in sets retirement.workPlans[id].plan: true; a printed match above 0 sets
  .match: true (DATA_MODEL updated, no version bump). A figure used from the stub drops any
  guess entry on the path it writes (clearGuess); a guess on file reads "(our guess)" and is
  never "already on file".
- alreadyOnFile: the same pay a year to the dollar, the same withholding, 401(k) money, match,
  balance or Social Security amount reads "Already on file. Nothing to change." with no button.
- One filled button: the first change not used yet; the others are outlined.
- New income line for the unnamed first adult is "Your pay" (was "Me's pay").

view.js touched: modules/ai/reader/view.js (the ?kind=paystub&person= landing, the pay stub
intro and box, "How often are you paid?", the 401(k) proposal words, "Already on file", the
notice where "Use it" was tapped, one filled "Use it").

